{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.3,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "extra_component",
      "components": ["J10"],
      "pins": ["J10.2", "U11.1", "U11.2", "U7.13", "D4.2"],
      "nets": ["/Microcontroller/NET0011", "GND"],
      "observed": "J10, a 2-pin screw terminal, has pin 2 on the same net as ESP32 GPIO1 (/Microcontroller/NET0011), the TPS1H200AQDGNRQ1 IN and DIAG_EN pins, and the heater-indicator LED anode. Pin 1 is on GND. This net is the heater-switch control line, and J10 provides an external connection point onto it.",
      "expected": "The specification lists the board's connectors (thermocouple inputs, fan headers, barrel jack, USB-C, heater output) and describes the heater control net as driven only by ESP32 GPIO1. It does not mention any external terminal on that net.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"6\") (name \"/Microcontroller/NET0011\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"J10\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"Pin_2\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"IN\") (pintype \"input\")) (node (ref \"U11\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"DIAG_EN\") (pintype \"input\")) (node (ref \"U7\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"GPIO1/ADC1_CH1/XTAL_32K_N\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "`IN`/`DIAG_EN` (pins 1/2) are both driven from ESP32 GPIO1 (net `/Microcontroller/HEATER`)"}
      ],
      "impact": "An external connection to the heater-enable node could override or disturb the MCU's control of the heater switch, or inject noise into a fault-critical input. Its purpose is undocumented.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    },
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["U2"],
      "pins": ["U2.9", "U2.12"],
      "nets": ["GND"],
      "observed": "The TPS2121RUXR status pin ST (pin 9) is tied directly to GND, the same net as the device's GND pin (pin 12). ST is an output pin in the netlist.",
      "expected": "The ST status output should be left floating or pulled up through a resistor to a logic rail, so the status signal can change state. Tying an output to ground makes the status permanently asserted and cannot report anything.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"9\") (pinfunction \"ST\") (pintype \"output\"))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "`ST`(pin9)/`GND`(pin12) go to `GND`."}
      ],
      "impact": "Power-mux status information is lost. The device's status output is held low permanently, so any fault or switchover indication cannot be seen. This is a functional deviation from normal use, though it is unlikely to damage the board.",
      "confidence": 0.2
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist is largely internally consistent: pin assignments, rails and passive values match standard practice and the spec's values. The only candidate deviations are an undocumented screw terminal J10 tied onto the heater-enable node and the TPS2121 ST output tied to ground, both low confidence, so the verdict is uncertain."
}

